<title>GERMANY: German govt to sell Lufthansa stake in H2.</title>
<headline>German govt to sell Lufthansa stake in H2.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government said on Tuesday its remaining 36 percent stake, worth some three billion marks ($1.9 billion), in German airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG would be sold in one go in the second half of this year.</p>
<p>A government spokesman said the new draft law applying to share ownership of airline businesses would allow a flotation of the stake within that timeframe.</p>
<p>The government will seek to float the stake in one go, rather than in steps, to maximise its potential return on the sale.</p>
<p>Lufthansa earlier said it thought the sale of the stake was likely in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.589 German Marks)</p>
</text>
